WEBVTT

00:23:57.792 --> 00:24:01.726
It's not a problem,
it's in the nature of relationships

00:24:01.750 --> 00:24:03.601
that you're going to do breaches.

00:24:03.625 --> 00:24:05.101
Betrayal is a different story,

00:24:05.125 --> 00:24:09.792
and I think that betrayal lives
in the shadow of trust all the time.

00:24:10.375 --> 00:24:12.726
So the first thing is the acknowledgment,

00:24:12.750 --> 00:24:15.893
and it involves an element
of remorse or guilt sometimes

00:24:15.917 --> 00:24:17.893
for what you've done to the other person,

00:24:17.917 --> 00:24:19.726
not necessarily for your own action.

00:24:19.750 --> 00:24:22.809
The second one, what you call
responsibility in the rebuilding,

00:24:22.833 --> 00:24:24.184
I call it the vigilante.

00:24:24.208 --> 00:24:28.684
It's like you show the benevolence
of that the relationship matters to you.

00:24:28.708 --> 00:24:31.476
Because a breach of trust
says to the other person